cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Elench in academic work, please cite it as below."

title: "Elench: A Cost-Contract Language and Static Verification Framework for AI-Generated Code"
abstract: >-
  Elench is a programming language designed for AI code generation.
  Instead of asking whether generated code is correct, it asks whether the
  generated code's *cost* stays inside a declared contract. Every function
  carries a cost signature derived by static analysis over a symbolic value
  domain; candidates for the same task are measured and dispatched by input
  size; and the whole toolchain emits machine-readable cost signatures so that
  an agent can treat cost as a budget prior rather than an afterthought.

